  "question": {
    "text": "A positive acute angle is divided into two parts whose tangents are $\\frac{1}{2}$ and $\\frac{1}{3}$. Then the angle is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$\\pi / 4$",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\pi / 5$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\pi / 3$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\pi / 6$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Hints : Angle $\\theta=\\tan ^{-1} \\frac{1}{2}+\\tan ^{-1} \\frac{1}{3}=\\tan ^{-1}\\left(\\frac{\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{3}}{1-\\frac{1}{2} \\cdot \\frac{1}{3}}\\right)$\n$=\\tan ^{-1}\\left(\\frac{5 / 6}{5 / 6}\\right)=\\tan ^{-1}(1)=\\pi / 4$"
  }
